STATUS

The core hypothesis of this disclosure — that delta signals are less sensitive
to slide-level batch effects than static signals — is UNVALIDATED. Section 4 of
README.md records the negative experimental evidence verbatim, including a static
H&E-to-HER2 classification that failed on a 17-slide dataset (validation tile-level
AUC 0.27, slide-level AUC 0.25), slide-identity classification at AUC 1.0000,
train-versus-validation domain discrimination at AUC 0.9995, a slide-identity AUC
that moved only from 0.9994 to 0.9995 under Macenko normalisation, static virtual
staining SFS of 0.445 (0.526 after histogram matching), and a condition sensitivity
L1 of 0.0112.

That evidence is retained deliberately. A defensive publication is useful to the
extent that it is technically credible, and it is credible only if it reports what
failed.


